{
  "_comment": "Source -> docs coupling map for Politicas. When a turn edits source matching an entry's sourceGlobs with user- or contributor-visible effect (new/removed route, changed module architecture, new command, design-token or lint-rule change, sample-data-layer status), update the coupled doc in the SAME change. Internal-only edits (refactors, bugfixes with no behavior shift) need no doc update. A single source glob may couple to several docs. Globs are scoped to the contexts in context-map.json (25 contexts / 9 groups). Deliberately NOT listed here: dated, append-only or point-in-time artifacts that must never be retro-edited to match new code - docs/harness/** (the 2026-07-26 combined scan snapshot), docs/architect/decisions|scans/** (ADRs and scan records), docs/data-analysis/case-*/** batch notes and the vault ledgers (coverage-ledger, graph-log, frontier, patterns, contradictions), and the docs/data-analysis/justice-sources-* / cluster-* / phase* research notes. Those are history, not documentation of current source.",
